# PX4 params for GPS-denied flight on ZED Mini VIO (sim + real, docs/hardware.md,
# docs/interface-contract.md, .claude/skills/zed-contract/SKILL.md). Scenario: `px4.params: [ekf2_vision, ...]`.
# Values verified against the pinned firmware source (PX4_TAG, ADR-003):
# /opt/PX4-Autopilot/src/modules/ekf2/{module,params_external_vision,params_gnss,params_magnetometer}.yaml
#
# SITL: applied at PX4 boot by the launcher (scenario `px4.params`, docker/sim/configs/single_iris_vio.yaml).
# scripts/push_px4_params.py can still push it to a running PX4, but EKF2_HGT_REF/EKF2_MAG_TYPE are
# reboot_required and a SITL reboot is refused — pushing alone leaves EKF2 on its GPS-anchored origin.
#
# Format (scripts/push_px4_params.py, NOT the QGC 5-column save format):
#   NAME  VALUE  MAV_PARAM_TYPE
# MAV_PARAM_TYPE: 6 = INT32 (enum/bitmask params below are stored as int32 in PX4),
#                 9 = REAL32 (float params).
#
# EV_POS_X/Y/Z = vision sensor lever arm (body FRD, m). The ZED wrapper's odometry is the pose of zed_camera_link, not base_link
# (its base frame is hard-wired, interface-contract.md R3), and the zed-bridge relays it unchanged: EKF2 must take the camera
# offset out itself. Value = the mount `positional_tracking.initial_base_pose` in docker/zed/zed.yaml (FLU [0.18, 0, -0.02] ->
# FRD [0.18, 0, 0.02]); the real drone's mount goes here too once measured (docs/hardware.md).

EKF2_HGT_REF   3   6   # Vision (0=Baro 1=GPS 2=Range 3=Vision)
EKF2_EV_CTRL   15  6   # bit0 hpos + bit1 vpos + bit2 3D vel + bit3 yaw (hardware.md: "15 pos+vel+yaw+hgt")
EKF2_EV_DELAY  0   9   # ms. The sample stamp already is the capture time: in the sim the zed-bridge restamps on arrival minus
                       # the measured camera->bridge latency (zed.yaml sim: restamp_latency_ms, B17); on the drone the wrapper
                       # stamps with image capture time. EKF2 subtracts EV_DELAY on top, so a non-zero value double-counts it.
EKF2_EV_POS_X  0.18 9  # camera lever arm, see the note above
EKF2_EV_POS_Y  0.0  9
EKF2_EV_POS_Z  0.02 9
EKF2_GPS_CTRL  0   6   # GPS fusion fully disabled (indoor / GPS-denied)
EKF2_MAG_TYPE  5   6   # None — EV supplies yaw (EKF2_EV_CTRL bit3); avoids mag/vision yaw fighting
